# MEASUREMENT PROBE — origin 2 split by head constant, and the operand census.
# Worktree-only, never to be landed.
#
# `git apply scripts/nat-major-probe.diff` onto a scratch worktree, then
#
#   cargo build --release --features tg,stepcount --bin nanoda_bin
#   ./target/release/nanoda_bin cfg.json                       # censuses, side-effect free
#   NANODA_ASSUME='accelerated Nat op at LITERAL' …            # delete Nat.ble at literals
#   NANODA_ASSUME='accelerated Nat op, operands not literal' … # delete Nat.beq, the rest
#   NANODA_ASSUME='accelerated Nat op' …                       # both
#   NANODA_ASSUME='major premise is not a constructor' …       # the OfNat.ofNat residue
#   NANODA_NAT_CMP_MIN=256 …                                   # withhold GMP beq/ble under 256
#
# `cfg.json` is `good/init-prelude.ndjson`, `nat_extension` and
# `string_extension` on, `num_threads: 1`, `unsafe_permit_all_axioms`.
# `NANODA_ASSUME` is the tree's own deletion knob (`origin_assume`), which
# matches an origin by substring; this probe only has to split the reason
# string for it to become deletable per constituent.
#
# What it adds:
#
#   * `derive_iota_core` returns THREE reason strings where it returned one, so
#     `origin_bit` gives each its own bit and the sub-tree column prices each
#     separately: an accelerated `Nat` op at literal operands, the same at
#     non-literal operands, and the residue. The split is read off `NameCache` —
#     the same pointers `try_reduce_nat` matches — not off a spelling.
#   * `NAT_MAJOR` / `NAT_INST` — the firings by operand *shape* and by operand
#     *value*, which is what refuted the brief: 55 distinct `Nat.ble` instances,
#     every operand <= 12.
#   * `CMP_BITS` — every accelerated `Nat.beq`/`ble` the run performs, bucketed
#     by operand bit width. 612 of 643 are <= 4 bits.
#   * `NANODA_NAT_CMP_MIN` — withholds the GMP acceleration below a threshold so
#     the comparison unfolds structurally instead. The deletion measurement for
#     "is the acceleration what blocks this origin". It is not: the origin is
#     unchanged at 466 own / 3 161 sub-tree, and the ledger is 148 gaps worse.
#
# Ledger byte-identical with the censuses in and no environment variable set:
# 15 734 gaps, 2 232 escapes, 159 803 derived — at `c31c707` where the numbers
# were taken and again at `71b608a` after origin 1 was split.
